 in stage3 was introduced. But there is no description in stage2. The remaining case seems to be for cases where an RLF report is not provided from another gNB or in cases where the network chooses not to download or is unable to obtain the RLF report from the UE. This means there is no point in restricting the usage on e.g. UE support. This may lead to duplicated error reports, if the network will provide the failure indication with and without RLF report, but this resolution can be handled in the involved nodes and there is no need to capture this resolution in the spec. Therefore, it is proposed to capture a new, simple statement that the forwarding to the gNB-DU may be triggered by UE re-establishing or recovering after failure or by receiving a Failure Indication without any RLF report. Summary of change: Added the description of the behaviour in the intermediate node (gNB-CU) in case of failure report without RLF report. Consequences if not approved: No stage2 text describing the behaviour in the intermediate node in case of failure report without RLF report.
